{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\ni=d['interpretations'][0]\ni['experiment_id']='9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-experiment'\ni['investigation_id']='9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0'\ni['conclusion']='violated'\ni['defect_claim']='asserted'\ni['executions']={'430d7ba602ed4666bdfe63a96c71e2fc':[1]}\ni['rationale']=(\\\"Observed in the retained execution: after restart with RestoreCommittedLogs=true and no snapshot, the node's configuration is empty \\\"\n \\\"(event index 1: mode=restore_on_no_snapshot, servers_before=1, servers_after=0, config_preserved=false, snapshot_count=0, staged_commit=6, log_last_index=7) \\\"\n \\\"and it never campaigns again (became_leader=false after a 3s opportunity, with the node logging 'no known peers, aborting election'), while the two controls keep the configuration and re-elect \\\"\n \\\"(index 3 restore_off_no_snapshot: servers_after=1, became_leader=true; index 5 restore_on_with_snapshot: servers_after=1, snapshot_count=1, became_leader=true). \\\"\n \\\"Source account of the mechanism: NewRaft documents that existing state such as logs and peers is restored (api.go 504-507) and RestoreCommittedLogs is documented only as replaying committed logs before startup (config.go 243-254); \\\"\n \\\"restoreFromCommittedLogs raises lastApplied to the persisted commit index (api.go 723-755) and the configuration scan then starts at max(lastSnapshot,lastApplied)+1 (api.go 611-613), so configuration entries inside the committed prefix are never turned into r.configurations \\\"\n \\\"by their only producer processConfigurationLogEntry (raft.go 1605-1623) unless a snapshot carries them (api.go 645-689). With Servers empty, runFollower refuses to start an election (raft.go 230-234) and both vote handlers skip their membership checks (raft.go 1663-1672, 1780-1784).\\\")\ni['counterevidence']=[\n \\\"The repository's own TestRaft_RestoreCommittedLogs (raft_test.go 1183-1280) passes because it always snapshots before restarting; the executed snapshot control (index 5) shows the same masking, so the failing case is specifically a configuration that lives only in the skipped committed log prefix.\\\",\n \\\"Restarting identical durable state with RestoreCommittedLogs=false keeps servers_after=1 and re-elects (index 3), so neither the commit-tracking store nor replaying logs to the FSM is the cause.\\\",\n \\\"The node still has all committed entries on disk (log_last_index=7 > commit_index=6), so this is a lost configuration context, not lost data; the entry itself is present and would be re-read only if a snapshot were installed.\\\"]\ni['limitations']=[\n \\\"Executed scope is a single-voter in-memory cluster (protocol version 3, heartbeat/election 50ms); the multi-node consequences (votes granted to servers the node cannot show it contains, quorum size and configuration changes computed from a stale base) are read from source and are the subject of the registered gap.\\\",\n \\\"The restart uses the commit index the store reported (6, log end 7); the boundary of the skipped prefix depends on that value, but the omission of the configuration entry does not.\\\",\n \\\"Nothing in the captured sources requires an application to snapshot before enabling RestoreCommittedLogs, so the failing condition is reachable through the documented configuration alone.\\\"]\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -5\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
