{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['sources'] += [\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"append_config_entry\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":1204,\\\"end_line\\\":1241,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"cfg_change_gate\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"raft.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":654,\\\"end_line\\\":664,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"configuration.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":328,\\\"end_line\\\":406,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n]\nd['experiment2']=None\nd.pop('experiment2')\nd['experiment']=[d.pop('experiment')]\nd['experiment'].append({\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_gap_probe_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"append_config_entry\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"cfg_change_gate\\\",\\\"vote_config_checks\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\n  \\\"description\\\":\\\"Two-voter in-memory cluster {A,B}: A is bootstrapped with both voters and becomes leader, commands are committed, A takes a snapshot (configuration {A,B} at index 1), then AddVoter C commits a configuration entry at index 8 while A and B are the only running servers. Four further commands push the persisted commit index past index 8. A is shut down and restarted on the same stores with a fresh transport (case restore_on with RestoreCommittedLogs=true, control restore_off with it false). Observed: the restarted node's configuration membership versus the still-running peer's view and the newest configuration entry in its own log; then, while the restarted node is stably leader, one further AddVoter E and the resulting cluster configuration on both nodes.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\n   \\\"AddVoter C commits with acks from A and B only, which is a legal quorum of three voters; C is never started, so nothing else can observe C's absence.\\\",\n   \\\"The snapshot predates the configuration change, so it carries configuration {A,B} at index 1 while the newest configuration entry (index 8) is in the log.\\\",\n   \\\"The extra commands after the change are ordinary applications; they only advance the persisted commit index past the configuration entry, which any later commit would do.\\\"\n  ],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"Elections, partitions and failover among more than two servers are not exercised; the point is which configuration each node uses, not how leaders are chosen.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"peers\\\":2,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"trailing_logs\\\":10}\n },\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap of both voters on A, real election, real applies, real user snapshot on A, real AddVoter C through the cluster, real shutdown and restart of A on the same InmemCommitTrackingStore/InmemStore/InmemSnapshotStore. Nothing is fabricated: the log, snapshot metadata and staged commit index all come from those operations, and the control case runs the identical procedure with RestoreCommittedLogs=false.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_gap_restore_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"pre_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"contains_c_before\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_gap_restore_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"pre_restart\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"contains_c_before\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_gap_change_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"post_restart_leader\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"stable_A_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"post_restart\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_gap_restore_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"servers_after\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"After restart with RestoreCommittedLogs enabled, the node must still know the newest committed configuration {A,B,C} that is present in its own log.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"post_restart\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_gap_restore_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"servers_after\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":3},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the same restart without RestoreCommittedLogs keeps all three members.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_config_change\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_gap_change_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"contains_c_final\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A configuration change issued by the restarted node must not remove voter C, which no request removed and which remains in the committed configuration.\\\"}\n ]\n})\nd['interpretations'].append({\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"append_config_entry\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"cfg_change_gate\\\"],\n \\\"conclusion\\\":\\\"explained\\\",\n \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":(\\\"Registered gap answered by source trace plus a construction-time run of this probe. Source: a restarted node adopts the snapshot's configuration whenever the newest configuration entry lies inside the skipped committed prefix (api.go 611-613 with 723-755, snapshot path api.go 645-689), and appendConfigurationEntry then computes the next configuration from that stale r.configurations.latest (raft.go 1204-1241) once configurationChangeChIfStable admits the change because latest and committed indexes look equal (raft.go 654-664); nextConfiguration derives the new membership from that same base (configuration.go 328-406). Observed at construction time (native run, pending retained receipt): with RestoreCommittedLogs=true the restarted node reports 2 servers while its peer still reports 3 and its own log's newest configuration entry (index 8) is below the persisted commit index (11); the next AddVoter then committed successfully (err=nil) with the cluster converging on 3 servers without C, so voter C was legitimately added and then silently removed without any request removing it. The control case with RestoreCommittedLogs=false kept 3 servers and the later change produced 4 members including C.\\\"),\n \\\"answers\\\":{\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-gap-0\\\":{\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"Yes for both parts, subject to the retained receipt for this probe: the stale configuration is adopted when the snapshot predates the committed configuration entry, and it does justify a different decision - a configuration change based on the stale membership drops voter C for the whole cluster (observed change_err=nil, both nodes ending with 3 members and contains_c=false), instead of the intended 4-member configuration. Source dependency chain recorded in the rationale; construction-time run reproduced all three predictions, retained execution pending.\\\",\\\"resolved\\\":False}},\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"The control case with RestoreCommittedLogs=false on identical stores preserved all three members and added E without dropping C, so the stale base is specific to the skipped committed prefix rather than to config changes in general.\\\"],\n \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"This is a construction-time native reproduction; the formal receipt for this harness is requested in this update and the claim is retained as explained/unresolved-for-receipt until it exists.\\\",\\\"C never runs, so the probe cannot show whether C would itself notice or resist its removal; that is about C's own state, not about the decision the restarted node made.\\\",\\\"The removal happens through a successful public AddVoter, so the consequence is reachable through the ordinary configuration API, but only while the restarted node is leader and its stale latest/committed indexes look equal.\\\"]\n})\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -5\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
